id #uuid "c3a59ed6-d085-5b13-8224-1899eb66db38" :question/math-academy-id "q-77956" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors ${i,j,k}$ of ${R}^{3}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j,k}$ are the first, second, and third columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j,k}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i,$ $T\\cdot j,$ and $T\\cdot k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T\\cdot k=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Images of the Standard Basis Vectors Under a Given Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f196b10c-641e-5ce2-9fcd-3d46e307a55d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, and $[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345302} {:answer/id #uuid "e0eb1c4b-5d0c-5c1e-b53b-78e511949c12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, $[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, and $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345303} {:answer/id #uuid "df8ec8be-83d6-5002-be89-c4e70b901522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, and $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345304} {:answer/id #uuid "c9c6191a-16bf-52ca-ae04-1442a5a74b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, and $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345305} {:answer/id #uuid "98fe58a7-561d-5deb-969e-ece258c81755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, and $[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98fe58a7-561d-5deb-969e-ece258c81755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, and $[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345306} :answer-field/id #uuid "18111578-c492-56fd-a07c-e4919a6f6d09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d760f8c-5521-5c50-bb26-dcdfa4a2f288" :question/math-academy-id "q-77959" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors ${i,j,k}$ of ${R}^{3}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j,k}$ are the first, second, and third columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j,k}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i,$ $T\\cdot j,$ and $T\\cdot k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T\\cdot k=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-