vectors of the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$, while ${i}^{′}$ and ${j}^{′}$ are their images under the linear transformation $T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that \n${i}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ \nand \n${j}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d028b4-e246-57fd-abc1-042968d680e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345316} {:answer/id #uuid "1e5777ac-c58e-546c-b1d3-541856b8ab48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345317} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a4de9d-938e-5e49-9080-3cb20964b39c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345318} {:answer/id #uuid "c023905e-683d-5430-873e-15d37177f41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345319} {:answer/id #uuid "3d5ee86f-9aea-5bd4-9586-82c7a93faae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345320}] :answer-field/